This version consolidates the material from the uploaded 96-page notes, removes repeated explanations, groups related topics together, and keeps the corrected versions already present in the notes. It is designed so that one read gives you a complete DBA revision map.
Source basis: uploaded My_Notes.docx. The original notes cover PostgreSQL architecture, security, configuration, performance, indexes, MVCC, WAL, replication, backups/PITR, pgBackRest, PgBouncer, HA, AWS basics, troubleshooting, SQL fundamentals and interview questions.
How to use this document
•	First pass: read headings + ⭐ memory lines.
•	Second pass: read the tables and interview answers.
•	Before an interview: revise the Last-Minute Cheat Sheet and Scenario-Based Answers.
•	If asked for details, expand from the relevant section instead of trying to memorize every command.
